@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Create an email ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cannot access email",
  "description": "User cannot log in to the company email account.",
  "category": "Email",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "amir@example.com"
}

### Return all tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets

### Filter tickets by status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=OPEN

### Filter tickets by priority
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?priority=HIGH

### Filter tickets by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?category=Email

### Return one ticket (replace with an ID returned above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/REPLACE_WITH_TICKET_ID

### Return paged tickets (page 0, size 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5

### Return paged tickets (page 1, size 5)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=1&size=5

### Return paged tickets sorted desc by createdAt
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=createdAt&direction=desc

### Invalid status value
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=INVALID

### Invalid priority value
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?priority=URGENT

### Page with no records
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=99&size=5

### Very large page size
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=100

### Unknown sort field
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/paged?page=0&size=5&sortBy=unknownField&direction=asc

### Combined filters (status and priority)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets?status=OPEN&priority=HIGH
